00:58:34,285 --> 00:58:40,285
The Crucible is a 1996 American historical drama film directed by Nicholas
Hytner and written by Arthur Miller, based on his 1953 play.

11
01:04:25,714 --> 01:04:31,714
It stars Daniel Day-Lewis as John Proctor, Winona Ryder as Abigail Williams, Paul Scofield in his final live-action film
role as Judge Thomas Danforth, Joan Allen as Elizabeth Proctor, and Bruce Davison as Reverend Samuel Parris.

12
01:10:17,142 --> 01:10:23,142
Set in 1692, during the Salem witch trials, the film follows a group of teenage girls who, after getting caught
performing a ritual in the woods, band together and falsely accuse several of the townspeople of witchcraft.

13
01:16:08,571 --> 01:16:14,571
Principal photography began in Massachusetts and Nova Scotia on
September 11, 1995, and concluded on November 18.

14
01:22:00,000 --> 01:22:06,000
The Crucible was theatrically released in the United States by 20th Century Fox on November 27, 1996,
and was a commercial failure, grossing only $7.3 million against its $25 million budget.

15
01:27:51,428 --> 01:27:57,428
Despite this, it received positive reviews from critics, with Day-Lewis, Ryder,
Scofield, and Allen earning widespread acclaim for their performances.

16
01:33:42,857 --> 01:33:48,857
The Crucible was screened at the 47th Berlin International Film
Festival, where it competed for the Golden Bear.

17
01:39:34,285 --> 01:39:40,285
At the 54th Golden Globe Awards, Scofield and Allen were nominated for Best Supporting Actor and Best Supporting Actress respectively, while Allen received a Best
Supporting Actress nomination at the 69th Academy Awards, and Scofield won Best Actor in a Supporting Role at the 50th British Academy Film Awards.

18
01:45:25,714 --> 01:45:31,714
Arthur Miller received nominations for the Academy Award for Best Adapted
Screenplay and the BAFTA Award for Best Adapted Screenplay.

